---
import AppLayout from '../../../../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import { chatLikeGenZ, appPath, studio, supportLink } from '../../../../data/apps';

const path = appPath(chatLikeGenZ);
const deletionEmail = supportLink('Chat Like Gen Z account and data deletion');
---

<AppLayout
  title="Chat Like Gen Z Account and Data Deletion | AppCrazy Labs"
  description="Request deletion of a Chat Like Gen Z account and associated data without signing in. Find your Support ID, email the developer, and understand current deletion limits."
  canonicalPath={`${path}data-deletion/`}
  heading="Chat Like Gen Z data deletion"
  kicker="AppCrazy Labs · Privacy & support"
  deck="Request deletion of your account and associated data. No sign-in is needed to contact us."
  backLabel={chatLikeGenZ.name}
  backHref={path}
>
  <div slot="meta" class="hero-actions">
    <a class="button button-primary" href={deletionEmail}>Email a deletion request ↗</a>
    <a class="text-link" href={`${path}privacy/`}>Privacy policy →</a>
  </div>

  <p>
    <strong>Chat Like Gen Z is developed by Sidhanshu Udawat under the AppCrazy Labs brand.</strong>
    The Android test app creates an anonymous Firebase account for your conversion
    balance, even if you do not link Google. You can start a deletion request from
    this page without opening the app or signing in.
  </p>

  <section id="request" aria-labelledby="request-title">
    <h2 id="request-title">How to request deletion</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Email <a href={deletionEmail}>{studio.email}</a> with the subject
        “Chat Like Gen Z account and data deletion”. The button above opens a draft.
      </li>
      <li>
        Include your Support ID if you have it. In the current Android test build,
        find it at <strong>Settings → Save or recover balance</strong>, under
        “Support / test account ID”. If you linked Google, also tell us the email
        address used for that link, preferably by writing from that address.
      </li>
      <li>
        Say whether you want your app account and associated records deleted,
        specific support messages removed, or both. If you no longer have the
        Support ID, explain that in your email so we can discuss another way
        to locate and verify the account.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Do not send your password, payment-card number, purchase token, Firebase
      credential, private message text or identity documents. We may request
      limited additional information to confirm that the account belongs to you.
      We will reply with the status, any verification needed, what can be removed
      and any records that must be retained. No fixed completion time has been
      verified for the current test process.
    </p>
  </section>

  <aside class="note-callout" aria-label="Account deletion options">
    <strong>Delete in the app, or ask support without signing in</strong>
    <p>
      Internal build 8 and later has <strong>Settings → Delete account &amp; data</strong>.
      Confirm your linked Google sign-in, if applicable, and then permanent deletion.
      This removes access to your account and unused conversions, including purchased
      conversions. It is irreversible and does not issue a Google Play refund. Older builds
      open an email draft; update or use the email request above.
    </p>
  </aside>
  <section aria-labelledby="verification-title">
    <h2 id="verification-title">How support verifies a request</h2>
    <p>
      For a linked account, support sends a one-time confirmation challenge to the verified
      Google email already registered on the Firebase account. Reply to that challenge with
      the code and explicit deletion confirmation. A supplied Support ID or an email From
      header alone is not proof of ownership. If you have no Support ID, support can locate
      the linked account using that verified email. The challenge expires after 24 hours.
    </p>
    <p>
      For an unlinked guest, use deletion from the signed-in app on the original device.
      If you have lost that device/session, support will discuss whether ownership can be
      safely established; a guest Support ID alone does not authorize deletion. We will not
      delete another person's records or ask for passwords, private tokens or identity papers.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="records-title">
    <h2 id="records-title">What is deleted</h2>
    <p>
      A confirmed request immediately blocks new conversions and grants on that account.
      Cleanup deletes the Firebase Authentication account and its Google identity link,
      wallet and balance, conversion records/results, pending requests, billing-account
      mappings, reward tickets and reward limits. Cleanup retries hourly if interrupted.
      Signing in to Google afterward cannot recover the deleted wallet; a new account can
      receive only its own new guest allowance. Your Google account itself stays intact.
    </p>
    <p>
      Support emails and attachments are handled separately. Say if you want those removed
      too; support removes matching correspondence after ownership verification and reports
      any specific retention exception. Email-provider backups and Google-managed transaction
      history are outside the app's account cleanup. Support replies with completion status;
      no fixed completion time for manual requests is promised.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="device-title">
    <h2 id="device-title">Data on your device</h2>
    <p>
      In-app deletion clears the writing profile, pending conversion input, recent saved
      input/result and pending reward state on the requesting phone, signs out Firebase,
      and attempts to revoke the app's Google sign-in access. This does not delete your
      Google account. If you requested deletion by email, or used other/offline devices,
      clear the app's storage on those devices to remove local copies. You can also remove
      Chat Like Gen Z from your Google Account's third-party connections if access remains.
    </p>
    <p>
      Uninstalling or clearing storage alone does not delete server data. Device backups,
      screenshots and text copied/shared to other apps may remain under their own controls.
      Never uninstall merely to request deletion; an unlinked guest may lose the ability
      to prove ownership. The app retains a local deletion-completion marker so it does not
      silently reopen the closed wallet; you may explicitly start a new guest account.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="retention-title">
    <h2 id="retention-title">What is retained, and for how long</h2>
    <p>
      After deletion, minimal purchase/reward records retain the transaction-token digest,
      pack/reward type, amount, timing and reversal status for 180 days. The Firebase UID,
      email, Google identity, ticket nonce and message data are removed. This supports
      duplicate-credit prevention and refund reconciliation. A hashed deletion receipt is
      kept for 90 days to block stale requests and record completion. Hourly cleanup removes
      these after the deadline, with possible delays during outages, retries or backlog.
      These periods are operational choices for internal testing, not stated legal mandates.
    </p>
    <p>
      For active accounts, conversion results and message fingerprints expire after seven
      days; the backend removes them on access and an hourly job performs physical cleanup.
      Minimal request/status records remain until account deletion to prevent duplicate
      deductions. Active pending requests settle or time out before cleanup. This does not
      promise physical deletion at exactly seven days. See the
      <a href={`${path}privacy/#retention`}>privacy policy</a> for local copies and service logs.
      Google Play, AdMob and Gemini manage data under their own policies; app deletion cannot
      erase Google's independent purchase or service records.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="contact-title">
    <h2 id="contact-title">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>App:</strong> Chat Like Gen Z<br />
      <strong>Legal developer / publisher:</strong> Sidhanshu Udawat<br />
      <strong>Privacy contact:</strong> Sidhanshu Udawat - <a href={deletionEmail}>{studio.email}</a>
    </p>
    <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-06">6 October 2026</time>.</p>
  </section>
</AppLayout>
